@* Every cover on every page renders through here, so none can show the browser's
   broken-image icon (design.md — Cover art): an image that fails to load gives way to the
   next candidate, and when none is left the caller's placeholder shows instead.

   The img's class and other attributes are the caller's, splatted on, so its look is
   unchanged; the caller's scoped CSS reaches the img only through ::deep, since this
   component renders it. The error handler names the source it was attached for, so a late
   error from a source already left behind changes nothing. *@

@if (_candidates.Current is { } source)
{
    <img src="@source" alt="" @attributes="AdditionalAttributes" @onerror="() => OnImageFailed(source)" />
}
else
{
    @ChildContent
}
